<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sisavang Vong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1959</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sisavang Vong was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Phrabang</a> from 1904 under French protection and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> from 1946 until his death in 1959. In 1945 he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against the Lao Issara movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phetsarath-ratanavongsa">Prince Phetsarath</a>, and under him Laos became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-union">French Union</a>, gaining full independence in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong.jpg" alt="Sisavang Vong" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified author of the publication (photographers, designers, etc. not credited). Booklet on the leaders, flags a... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roi_Sisavang_Vong_(crop_3x4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
